            <ArticleTitle>Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch Syndrome With Bilateral Tarsal Kink: Three Sutures for Correction.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SCS.0000000000003517</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe a 5-month-old male infant with Wiedemann-Rautenstrauch syndrome, which is an extremely rare condition. He had tarsal kink in upper eyelids in both eyes. The authors treated bilateral tarsal kink with an everting suture via a transconjunctival approach under local anesthesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
